    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "In my mind it was to match the name of the IS feature: automatic insights. So you write SQL queries to check for events that came via the \"automatic insights\" feature.\r\n\r\nI don't feel at all strongly about it though. If we happened to introduce something else that's automatic, that can have a suffix and the one without the suffix can mean \"came via the automatic insights feature\".",
    "commit_id": "5a49586d3feb1ccd95e7d0448e1c74f89b11d090",
